{
    "_doc": "ErAV NTR punishment chain, Part 1 + Part 2 (Plans/Plan_NTR_Punishment_MIA.md). debtclass_erav_kanon's onFailedEventID (ErAV/campaign.json) fires erav_ntr_punishment_kick when the monthly cycle fails to collect (Obligation_Debt.HandlePaymentEvent -> TradeManager.FireObligationEvent). The kick is deliberately silent and only starts the 'erav_ntr_punishment' event chain (StartEventChain, delayed a few minutes - Data/RaceDefs/nsfw_Labor_Events.json's 'labor' chain is the reference) so the interactive selection event doesn't land in the middle of the payment-resolve update batch and interrupt other running events. Like Data/Events/Obligation_Debt.json, the payer firing starts at the first entry (self = player) and the payee firing starts at the 'payee' labeled entry (self = Kiryu-gumi's manager, silent no-op so the chain is only ever started on the player). The chain then starts erav_ntr_punishment_select on self = player. Candidates: female, non-player members of ErAV_miyama_Household / ErAV_KiryuGumi_Filmstudio, excluding anyone still held in a locked party (isPartyLocked false - a previous victim still MIA; canMove is NOT usable here, the event runs at midnight while most NPCs sleep). Selection uses Options.forEachTargetKey (one option per candidate, $name$ interpolated, picked character bound as Targets[victim]). The player option references a target key that is never populated, so isValid fails and it renders greyed-out with invalidTooltip (same authored-disabled pattern as Opt_ArrangeJoin_Recreation's leave option). After the farewell kojo (GetKojoEntry - Kojo/ErAV_NTR_Punishment.json), StartEvent hands the victim to erav_ntr_mia_arrival (Part 2, self = victim) with the player injected as 'supervisor'. Part 2: arrival copies self into Targets[victim] (CopyTargets) and takes her into a new MIA party (CharaMIA) on expedition_erav_ntr_mia; she is released by its selfReleaseEventID erav_ntr_mia_release once her own expedition progress or the DurationHour countdown runs out (TeleportToFaction home, then ReleaseFromMIA). Both terminal paths (departure / no_candidates) call EndEventChain explicitly (same convention as nsfw_Labor_Events).",

