            {
                "ID": "erav_ntr_mia_arrival",
                "_comment": "Part 2/3 entry point. Self = victim, Targets[supervisor] = player (injected by Part 1's StartEvent). Setup branch copies self into Targets[victim] (CopyTargets - self is not a target key on its own) and rolls the client type once (RollWeighted into client_type). The pick branch has one option per type: AppendStringEquals gates on the rolled value, CharaMIA takes her into a new MIA party on that type's expedition def (Clients_nsfw/explorations.json), then jumps to that type's arrival narration. A failed CharaMIA (e.g. safe mode skips the nsfw folder, or a def ID typo) fails the option and falls through; all other types' AppendStringEquals are false, so execution lands on _generic -> the generic skeleton def expedition_erav_ntr_mia (its EventIDs are empty = countdown-only) -> arrival_generic. MIA faction is a placeholder (ErAV_KiryuGumi_Office) until the dedicated MIA faction is decided.",
